WEBVTT

00:00:18.792 --> 00:00:20.360
R...

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.129
Rose, I think you should
put down the newspaper

00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:26.566
at least while you're eating.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:29.467
Rose, you're a girl, so at least...

00:00:37.344 --> 00:00:40.880
Uh, um, what do you think
of today's breakfast?

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.083
I worked hard on it.

00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:45.381
Girls are difficult.

00:01:00.867 --> 00:01:01.959
I swear...

00:01:04.137 --> 00:01:08.775
It's not like I've acknowledged
that the old man's my father.

00:01:08.775 --> 00:01:10.810
It's not as easy as him
suddenly showing up

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:12.038
and saying he's my real father.

00:01:13.947 --> 00:01:16.616
I found my daughter, whom I'd
been looking for all this time...

00:01:16.616 --> 00:01:18.752
But it turned out to be Rose and...

00:01:18.752 --> 00:01:22.779
While I'm happy on one hand,
maybe I'm also taken aback by it.

00:01:25.492 --> 00:01:31.364
I am honestly happy that
Miss Rose is Mr. Roy's daughter.

00:01:31.364 --> 00:01:34.934
But they do not talk
to each other very much...

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:37.771
I would like for them
to get along better, but...

00:01:37.771 --> 00:01:39.439
I see...

00:01:39.439 --> 00:01:42.704
When did this place turn into
a counseling center anyway?

00:01:44.444 --> 00:01:52.185
You know the continuation of
the fairy tale I've wanted to hear about?

00:01:52.185 --> 00:01:58.920
If it's eternal happiness,
I'll forge it with my own hand

00:02:00.293 --> 00:02:10.270
It's like we were both seeking a
coincidence that was off by a page

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:12.439
And that's how fate brought us together

00:02:12.439 --> 00:02:20.613
More than those words
that you once kept to yourself

00:02:20.613 --> 00:02:29.522
It's the kindness that made you
keep them to yourself

00:02:29.522 --> 00:02:36.529
That I want to have faith in now

00:02:36.529 --> 00:02:44.237
You know, we'll be living
alongside uncertainty from now on

00:02:44.237 --> 00:02:50.643
We used to have nothing to lose,
but that's not us now

00:02:50.643 --> 00:02:58.351
You know the continuation of
the fairy tale I didn't know about before?

00:02:58.351 --> 00:03:04.624
If it's eternal happiness,
I'll forge it with my own hand

00:03:04.624 --> 00:03:08.526
It's something to build up bit by bit

00:03:22.941 --> 00:03:26.411
I see. So we failed to
apprehend the suspect.

00:03:26.411 --> 00:03:28.246
I am very sorry.

00:03:28.246 --> 00:03:33.718
Well, that's fine. This was an
irregular case for you guys anyway.

00:03:33.718 --> 00:03:36.054
How are Silvia and Celica doing?

00:03:36.054 --> 00:03:39.458
The word is, they should be
leaving the hospital in a week.

00:03:39.458 --> 00:03:41.493
I see.

00:03:41.493 --> 00:03:43.728
I'm sure it'll be tough for a while,

00:03:43.728 --> 00:03:46.798
but I ask that you and Accela
take care of matters in the meantime.

00:03:46.798 --> 00:03:47.599
That's all.

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:50.363
Yes, Sir. Please excuse me.

00:03:58.243 --> 00:03:59.744
It may have been irregular,

00:03:59.744 --> 00:04:03.148
but this case turned out
to be a good indicator.

00:04:03.148 --> 00:04:06.447
It means she is just what I expected.

00:04:18.597 --> 00:04:21.299
Oh, a bird...

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:23.835
You've got to be kidding me!

00:04:23.835 --> 00:04:28.907
Besides, so what if
that old man's my real father?!

00:04:28.907 --> 00:04:31.076
It's got nothing to do with me.

00:04:31.076 --> 00:04:33.237
You can't say it has
nothing to do with you.

00:04:34.279 --> 00:04:36.181
What do you think about all this?

00:04:36.181 --> 00:04:37.449
What do you mean?

00:04:37.449 --> 00:04:41.486
Do you really think
that old man's my father?

00:04:41.486 --> 00:04:43.355
All the circumstantial evidence points to it.

00:04:43.355 --> 00:04:46.057
But there's no scientific proof, right?!

00:04:46.057 --> 00:04:46.958
Even the genetic testing...

00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:52.063
We already know there are girls
whose genetic makeup mutated.

00:04:52.063 --> 00:04:53.498
I told you, remember?

00:04:53.498 --> 00:04:57.269
There is a possibility
that you are one of them.

00:04:57.269 --> 00:04:58.170
That's questionable.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:04:59.938
True.

00:04:59.938 --> 00:05:04.409
So about all that we can rely on
are those clothes and that shoe,

00:05:04.409 --> 00:05:07.845
and that song you've been humming
since you were little.

00:05:16.821 --> 00:05:20.358
That's not a song our parents
or I taught you.

00:05:20.358 --> 00:05:23.895
It's something you naturally started
to hum somewhere along the way.

00:05:23.895 --> 00:05:25.397
I heard from Roy

00:05:25.397 --> 00:05:30.502
that a record containing that song
has long been in his possession.

00:05:30.502 --> 00:05:34.573
In this day and age,
records are rare and valuable.

00:05:34.573 --> 00:05:36.131
It's most likely that...

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:49.287
Even so, those are only
circumstantial evidence.

00:05:49.287 --> 00:05:50.922
That's true.

00:05:50.922 --> 00:05:54.626
Well, regardless of whether
you're Roy's daughter or not,

00:05:54.626 --> 00:05:58.496
it doesn't change the fact
that you're our little sister.

00:05:58.496 --> 00:06:00.865
If you want to stay with Roy, you can.

00:06:00.865 --> 00:06:04.836
If you want to go back
to being a thief, you can.

00:06:04.836 --> 00:06:06.571
You can decide whatever you want.

00:06:06.571 --> 00:06:09.541
I'll go back! Of course, I'll go back!

00:06:09.541 --> 00:06:10.775
I see.

00:06:10.775 --> 00:06:14.346
Then are you going to be able
to achieve your original objective?

00:06:14.346 --> 00:06:16.481
Objective?

00:06:16.481 --> 00:06:17.573
Oh!

00:06:19.684 --> 00:06:21.686
Don't do something so stupid, Jeremy!

00:06:21.686 --> 00:06:24.556
U-Um, but... but... but I mean...

00:06:24.556 --> 00:06:26.258
Think it over!

00:06:26.258 --> 00:06:29.594
I definitely think your
research is interesting, but...

00:06:29.594 --> 00:06:31.997
But if I can complete my research,

00:06:31.997 --> 00:06:36.701
we can break the RUC's monopoly
on the energy market!

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:38.403
Don't you think that's compelling?!

00:06:38.403 --> 00:06:41.640
But what you're trying to do is too risky!

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:45.710
But, but, but I've already
completed the experimental apparatus

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.679
and the theory is ready, too!

00:06:47.679 --> 00:06:49.648
All I have left to do is prove it!

00:06:49.648 --> 00:06:51.383
Won't you help me?

00:06:51.383 --> 00:06:54.252
I can't knowingly let a friend
put herself in danger!

00:06:54.252 --> 00:06:54.919
Come on!

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:57.522
Reconsider, Jeremy.

00:06:57.522 --> 00:06:59.858
You coward!

00:06:59.858 --> 00:07:00.659
Jeremy?

00:07:00.659 --> 00:07:01.921
Hello? Jeremy?!

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.403
They're finally back together now...

00:07:19.311 --> 00:07:22.514
Hey, what are you doing in my room?!

00:07:22.514 --> 00:07:23.748
No, this is...

00:07:23.748 --> 00:07:24.516
Pervert.

00:07:24.516 --> 00:07:26.418
No, this is a misunderstanding!

00:07:26.418 --> 00:07:28.219
I'm leaving this place.

00:07:28.219 --> 00:07:29.354
- What?!
- Bye.

00:07:29.354 --> 00:07:30.388
Wait, Rita!

00:07:30.388 --> 00:07:32.754
I am Rose Anderson!

00:07:40.265 --> 00:07:41.755
Rose!

00:07:42.934 --> 00:07:44.736
Mr. Roy.

00:07:44.736 --> 00:07:46.465
Oh, um...

00:07:47.872 --> 00:07:50.241
Things just don't work like they used to...

00:07:50.241 --> 00:07:51.538
What?

00:08:03.088 --> 00:08:05.523
Roy! I'd like to talk to you
about something.

00:08:05.523 --> 00:08:08.193
Would you be able to take a job from me?

00:08:08.193 --> 00:08:10.362
Are your parents still around?

00:08:10.362 --> 00:08:11.796
What?

00:08:11.796 --> 00:08:14.099
Yes... they're well.

00:08:14.099 --> 00:08:17.268
Go home once in a while and let them
see you're doing all right.

00:08:17.268 --> 00:08:19.671
- What?
- Be good to your parents.

00:08:19.671 --> 00:08:22.401
P-Please wait a minute, Roy!

00:08:30.248 --> 00:08:34.619
I like both Mr. Roy and Miss Rose.

00:08:34.619 --> 00:08:38.289
So I am honestly happy that
they are father and daughter.

00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:41.826
I understand Mr. Roy
worries about Miss Rose,

00:08:41.826 --> 00:08:43.453
but he could pay a little...

00:08:45.997 --> 00:08:49.262
That was not good. What a failure.

00:08:51.536 --> 00:08:56.107
But he could pay a little attention
to what I say as well.

00:08:56.107 --> 00:08:57.972
Is it selfish to think so?

00:09:04.983 --> 00:09:07.185
What a great failure...

00:09:07.185 --> 00:09:09.154
Found you, Solty!

00:09:09.154 --> 00:09:10.054
Miss Rose?

00:09:10.054 --> 00:09:13.291
Sheesh! I went all the way
to the apartment looking for you

00:09:13.291 --> 00:09:16.528
and I bumped into the old man.
What a disaster!

00:09:16.528 --> 00:09:18.897
Uh, um, what is the matter?

00:09:18.897 --> 00:09:20.198
Oh, right, right.

00:09:20.198 --> 00:09:22.700
I have a little something
I want to talk to you about.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:23.724
Talk to me?

00:09:25.069 --> 00:09:26.771
What? You are leaving?!

00:09:26.771 --> 00:09:30.742
Yup. And remember how my
first objective in coming here

00:09:30.742 --> 00:09:33.578
was to bring you into our group?

00:09:33.578 --> 00:09:38.016
So, I've decided to
take you with me. Okay?

00:09:38.016 --> 00:09:42.253
"Okay"? Why is it that you are leaving?

00:09:42.253 --> 00:09:47.192
Why else? It's because
that old man's irritating.

00:09:47.192 --> 00:09:49.894
Besides, I haven't been working
during this recent stretch,

00:09:49.894 --> 00:09:52.263
so it's a perfect time
for me to take my leave.

00:09:52.263 --> 00:09:54.799
Will you not reconsider at all?

00:09:54.799 --> 00:09:56.968
Nope, nope. There's no way I would.

00:09:56.968 --> 00:10:01.172
But for Mr. Roy, you...
or I suppose, Miss Rita is...

00:10:01.172 --> 00:10:02.507
At any rate, he has been
looking for you all this time.

00:10:02.507 --> 00:10:04.576
You're gonna give me that crap, too?!

00:10:04.576 --> 00:10:05.910
Give me a break, all right?!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.849
- I'm Rose! I'm that
old man's daughter?! Get real!
- What?

00:10:10.849 --> 00:10:13.117
Come on, enough about that, okay?

00:10:13.117 --> 00:10:15.420
I'm going to get our stuff together,
so help me out.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.822
I refuse!

00:10:17.822 --> 00:10:21.092
I refuse. I will not go with you.

00:10:21.092 --> 00:10:23.461
W-Wait, Solty...

00:10:23.461 --> 00:10:25.597
Why are you so selfish?

00:10:25.597 --> 00:10:28.733
What is wrong with having
Mr. Roy care about you?!

00:10:28.733 --> 00:10:30.667
What are you so dissatisfied with?!

00:10:35.573 --> 00:10:37.709
What's your problem?! Fine, then!

00:10:37.709 --> 00:10:40.044
If that's how you're going to be, fine!

00:10:40.044 --> 00:10:45.482
Well, it won't hurt if I take a valuable
as a parting gift, right?

00:10:48.653 --> 00:10:53.181
What's going on Solty?
I heard some raised voices...

00:10:54.359 --> 00:10:56.160
Ms. Miranda...

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:57.991
Solty?

00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:36.967
Rose...

00:11:41.406 --> 00:11:43.107
Wh-What?

00:11:43.107 --> 00:11:47.745
You know, I'm thinking of doing
Roy's birthday party all over again.

00:11:47.745 --> 00:11:48.746
What?

00:11:48.746 --> 00:11:50.441
I'll be counting on your help, okay?

00:12:03.094 --> 00:12:05.697
Who is this?

00:12:05.697 --> 00:12:07.398
Mr. Roy Revant.

00:12:07.398 --> 00:12:10.702
He's a hunter with the
Maverick Hunters Office.

00:12:10.702 --> 00:12:11.536
A hunter?!

00:12:11.536 --> 00:12:13.371
Yeah, and...

00:12:13.371 --> 00:12:15.106
W-Wait, Jeremy!

00:12:15.106 --> 00:12:17.475
I'm sorry! I'm sorry, I'm sorry!

00:12:17.475 --> 00:12:20.612
I don't want to talk to anyone
unless they're intellectuals.

00:12:20.612 --> 00:12:23.014
- What?!
- I don't want to catch the stupid bug!

00:12:23.014 --> 00:12:24.015
Jeremy!

00:12:24.015 --> 00:12:26.718
- Jeremy, Roy isn't like that at all!
- L-I mean, I mean, being a hunter is
a physical sort of occupation, right?

00:12:26.718 --> 00:12:28.319
- Come on, listen to me!
- L-I mean, I mean, being a hunter is
a physical sort of occupation, right?

00:12:28.319 --> 00:12:30.583
- Jeremy! Jeremy!
- So, I'm sorry!

00:12:31.589 --> 00:12:32.690
Roy!

00:12:32.690 --> 00:12:35.921
If she's your friend,
do something about it yourself.

00:12:48.806 --> 00:12:51.843
The Aurora Wave is exerting
a strong influence today

00:12:51.843 --> 00:12:55.546
and several areas are prone
to electromagnetic interference.

00:12:55.546 --> 00:12:58.983
More like, you were still
planning on doing the party?

00:12:58.983 --> 00:13:00.018
Of course!

00:13:00.018 --> 00:13:04.288
You know, I think you've heard,
but I'm leaving soon!

00:13:04.288 --> 00:13:07.925
So why do I have to join in throwing
a celebration for someone else?

00:13:07.925 --> 00:13:09.794
That's exactly why.

00:13:09.794 --> 00:13:12.797
We'll do your farewell party
at the same time. Okay?

00:13:12.797 --> 00:13:14.966
Lumping it in together
doesn't make it all right!

00:13:14.966 --> 00:13:18.402
It's the children's duty
to humor the adults!

00:13:23.274 --> 00:13:25.710
Um, Miss Rose...

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:26.444
What?

00:13:26.444 --> 00:13:28.646
I am sorry about earlier.

00:13:28.646 --> 00:13:29.747
I was, well...

00:13:29.747 --> 00:13:31.215
It's not like...

00:13:31.215 --> 00:13:32.316
...it's bothering me.

00:13:32.316 --> 00:13:33.251
But...

00:13:33.251 --> 00:13:36.354
So, what do I have to do?

00:13:36.354 --> 00:13:40.024
Could you go out again
to buy Roy's present?

00:13:40.024 --> 00:13:41.325
All right.

00:13:41.325 --> 00:13:42.427
It doesn't matter what I get, right?

00:13:42.427 --> 00:13:43.795
Miss Rose.

00:13:43.795 --> 00:13:45.897
I'm really not bothered by it.

00:13:45.897 --> 00:13:48.066
It's not that I'm mad or anything.

00:13:48.066 --> 00:13:51.524
I just don't understand
my own feelings on it very well.

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:53.960
Miss Rose...

00:13:56.274 --> 00:13:57.571
Sorry.

00:14:01.379 --> 00:14:04.115
I guess it's hard to get things worked out.

00:14:04.115 --> 00:14:06.083
Oh, but that's life.

00:14:12.824 --> 00:14:14.592
Sarah...

00:14:14.592 --> 00:14:17.925
I found Rita, just as I promised.

00:14:19.397 --> 00:14:21.666
Rita was...

00:14:21.666 --> 00:14:23.327
...alive.

00:14:25.103 --> 00:14:28.334
But it seems she hates me now.

00:14:34.879 --> 00:14:36.710
She's alive.

00:14:38.816 --> 00:14:40.613
Thank goodness.

00:14:46.557 --> 00:14:48.426
Are you serious about doing this?

00:14:48.426 --> 00:14:49.227
Yes.

00:14:49.227 --> 00:14:50.461
Think it over!

00:14:50.461 --> 00:14:55.299
But, but see, they said the Aurora Wave's
influence is strong today!

00:14:55.299 --> 00:14:57.502
It's perfect for my experiment!

00:14:57.502 --> 00:14:59.070
Jeremy, no matter what you say, I...

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:02.840
What?! If you're not going to help me,
you're in the way, so go away.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.743
Then I'm calling the RUC.

00:15:05.743 --> 00:15:09.280
Since it looks like I have no choice,
but to get you arrested to stop you.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.448
Yuto!

00:15:10.448 --> 00:15:12.177
It's for your own good.

00:15:18.322 --> 00:15:21.926
Oh, my, my, you're still conscious
after getting hit by that?

00:15:21.926 --> 00:15:24.295
You're amazing, Yuto!

00:15:24.295 --> 00:15:25.630
J-Jeremy...

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:26.497
But you see,

00:15:26.497 --> 00:15:29.267
I want you to stay asleep
until I finish the experiment.

00:15:29.267 --> 00:15:30.666
I'm sorry.

00:15:33.571 --> 00:15:35.306
Oh, welcome back.

00:15:35.306 --> 00:15:37.842
What's this? You guys were all here?

00:15:37.842 --> 00:15:40.278
Where's Ri... Rose?

00:15:40.278 --> 00:15:42.713
I sent her out shopping for me.

00:15:42.713 --> 00:15:45.183
What if she just doesn't come back?

00:15:45.183 --> 00:15:49.987
There is no way that will happen!
Miss Rose will return, without fail!

00:15:49.987 --> 00:15:53.184
I was joking! It was a joke! Come on!

00:16:06.204 --> 00:16:07.171
It's me.

00:16:07.171 --> 00:16:09.173
R-Roy...

00:16:09.173 --> 00:16:11.409
Oh, it's you, Yuto.

00:16:11.409 --> 00:16:13.010
I'm sorry.

00:16:13.010 --> 00:16:14.812
P-Please help me.

00:16:14.812 --> 00:16:16.370
What's wrong, Yuto?!

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:28.426
Well, this'll do, right?

00:16:28.426 --> 00:16:29.627
The person at the store even said

00:16:29.627 --> 00:16:33.791
that this kind of present
is best for a middle-aged man.

00:16:36.667 --> 00:16:39.770
...his need to vent his rage at
not being able to find his daughter.

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:43.808
You know she's got to be dead already.

00:16:43.808 --> 00:16:46.577
But this time, I'll stay with you.

00:16:46.577 --> 00:16:47.511
Wait, Rita!

00:16:47.511 --> 00:16:49.280
...having Mr. Roy care about you!

00:16:49.280 --> 00:16:51.077
What are you so dissatisfied with?!

00:16:53.651 --> 00:16:57.088
I swear! What's up with them all?!

00:16:57.088 --> 00:16:58.456
I mean, I can't help it!

00:16:58.456 --> 00:17:01.859
It's not like I remember and it's not
like I feel like he's my father!

00:17:01.859 --> 00:17:04.061
No matter what anyone says to me,
I'm still me!

00:17:04.061 --> 00:17:06.427
There's no way to change that!

00:17:09.467 --> 00:17:12.169
That's right! I'm me!

00:17:12.169 --> 00:17:16.274
Why didn't I realize something
this simple?! It's so stupid!

00:17:16.274 --> 00:17:18.208
Ahahahaha, so there!

00:17:20.978 --> 00:17:25.082
Jeremy's trying to rebel against the RUC.

00:17:25.082 --> 00:17:26.384
What?!

00:17:26.384 --> 00:17:31.956
The RUC manages the energy, water,
and even the politics of this city

00:17:31.956 --> 00:17:34.058
to control the people.

00:17:34.058 --> 00:17:36.394
And we researchers

00:17:36.394 --> 00:17:41.198
are limited by the RUC concerning
what topics we can research.

00:17:41.198 --> 00:17:44.902
Jeremy's research topic is energy theory.

00:17:44.902 --> 00:17:46.103
When you go above the altitude

00:17:46.103 --> 00:17:49.774
stipulated by the law on
altitude limitations, lightning occurs

00:17:49.774 --> 00:17:51.309
and she wants to efficiently
collect that energy

00:17:51.309 --> 00:17:53.945
and turn it into a new source of energy.

00:17:53.945 --> 00:17:59.483
She's trying to break the RUC's monopoly
on the market by doing so!

00:17:59.483 --> 00:18:03.854
But if she tries it
and something goes wrong...

00:18:03.854 --> 00:18:04.956
You don't mean...

00:18:04.956 --> 00:18:08.289
Yes. There could be another Blast Fall.

00:18:18.202 --> 00:18:20.805
Oh, man, it's started to rain.

00:18:20.805 --> 00:18:22.739
This rain is so annoying.

00:18:27.578 --> 00:18:29.011
That must be the place.

00:18:43.894 --> 00:18:45.293
Over here!

00:18:49.533 --> 00:18:51.502
Damn, I can't get up there.

00:18:51.502 --> 00:18:52.570
You go ahead!

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:54.105
All right.

00:18:54.105 --> 00:18:56.440
- Hey, you guys!
- Rose!

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:58.743
- What are you doing up there?!
- What are you doing here?!

00:18:58.743 --> 00:19:01.178
- No, you have to hurry up
and get away from here!
- This is perfect!

00:19:01.178 --> 00:19:03.447
There's something I want
to talk to you about!

00:19:03.447 --> 00:19:04.415
Make it later!

00:19:04.415 --> 00:19:05.883
Just listen to me!

00:19:05.883 --> 00:19:07.578
Switch, on!

00:19:09.754 --> 00:19:11.745
I'll acknowledge it!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:17.661
I'll acknowledge that I'm your daughter!

00:19:17.661 --> 00:19:19.652
Because, I have no choice
but to acknowledge it!

00:19:21.932 --> 00:19:27.171
But I'm not Rita Revant.
I'm Rose Anderson!

00:19:27.171 --> 00:19:29.440
But what does that change?!

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:31.175
It doesn't change anything!

00:19:31.175 --> 00:19:36.080
I'm a thief and you're a hunter.
What's wrong with that?!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:37.843
That's okay, right?!

00:19:40.951 --> 00:19:42.919
That's all I wanted to say!

00:19:49.393 --> 00:19:51.691
Yeah, that's fine.

00:19:55.566 --> 00:19:59.403
Whether you go back to being a thief
or you leave my apartment,

00:19:59.403 --> 00:20:00.905
I don't care!

00:20:00.905 --> 00:20:05.638
As long as you're alive,
that's all that matters to me.

00:20:11.315 --> 00:20:12.714
Oh...

00:20:14.785 --> 00:20:17.686
Then, there's no problem.

00:20:20.324 --> 00:20:22.326
It's almost to the stipulated altitude.

00:20:22.326 --> 00:20:23.327
What?!

00:20:23.327 --> 00:20:24.487
It is over for you!

00:20:42.780 --> 00:20:43.974
Mr. Roy!

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:34.755
Rita!

00:21:52.446 --> 00:21:57.250
On a clear day in the park

00:21:57.250 --> 00:22:00.187
Looking up at the sky

00:22:00.187 --> 00:22:08.595
There was a tiny little cloud
that almost vanished

00:22:11.431 --> 00:22:16.203
Letting the wind take us where it will

00:22:16.203 --> 00:22:19.139
We live freely

00:22:19.139 --> 00:22:25.169
We make our way,
walking a little at a time

00:22:27.180 --> 00:22:30.013
We're the same

00:22:31.952 --> 00:22:36.723
This precious time

00:22:36.723 --> 00:22:40.527
Each time we meet

00:22:40.527 --> 00:22:50.070
This feeling of not being alone
turns into kindness

00:22:50.070 --> 00:22:56.676
I can turn it into
the courage to believe in someone

00:22:56.676 --> 00:23:08.918
And surely, before I vanish
into the far reaches of that sky...

00:23:15.595 --> 00:23:18.899
And I'd finally gotten over my confusion...

00:23:18.899 --> 00:23:20.267
Rose...

00:23:20.267 --> 00:23:23.937
"But For the Darkness
that Blankets the Soul..."
Next time, "But For the Darkness
that Blankets the Soul..."

00:23:23.937 --> 00:23:25.461
"But For the Darkness
that Blankets the Soul..."
Farewell.
